@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] comment-only-contract-review
Automated contract reviews submit only `COMMENT` reviews pinned to the inspected PR head; they
never approve a PR or request changes.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-notifications
Contract edits and removals cc their owners at the contract; introductions do not. Each discovered
violation ccs the violated contract's `notify` recipients, without implicitly including its owners.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-callers
New or changed contracts trigger inspection of at most 24 distinct callers/references per affected
declaration, including each inspected caller's applicable contracts; limits materially affecting a
finding are disclosed in that finding's comment.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-summary
Review summaries are `cc: LGTM` when no violations are found, otherwise `cc:` followed by a blank
line and bullets of `**{contract-name}**: {failure_short_description}`, with details in the
associated comments.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-locations
Every review finding identifies the violating source location; locations outside the commentable
PR diff are retained in the review body with source permalinks.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] review-host-services
Review setup preserves permissions on host service sockets so the runner's DNS and reporting
services remain usable.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-requests
Reviews run on a standalone `r? cc` line, optionally with GitHub mentions between `r?` and `cc`,
in a new PR description or conversation comment, or an edit introducing that request. Draft PRs
are eligible; pushes and edits retaining an existing request do not request another review.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-request-access
Only human requesters with repository write access can trigger reviews of open PRs whose head
repository is this repository.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-request-identity
A fresh request can review unchanged commits; an already-published request with the same base/head
commits is skipped. Publishing skips closed PRs but remains pinned to the inspected head when new
commits arrive or the base changes; review context and comment locations use the captured comparison.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-automation-source
Review request handling, prompts, and publication use the workflow's revision; inspected source
uses the PR head captured when resolving the request.
